WHAT IS IN assets/ AND WHERE IT CAME FROM

Everything below is covered by the LICENCE file and may not be reused.

  assets/bonelight/    Generated by the Python tools in tools/art/. Drawn in
                       code against the palette contract in
                       .ai/art-direction.md, not painted by hand.

  assets/sfx/          Generated by tools/audio/. Synthesised, not recorded and
                       not sampled from any library.

  assets/kidsart/      DRAWN BY CHILDREN. Twelve sprite sheets made by my kids,
                       used exactly as drawn — cropped and repacked, never
                       repainted. They are the entire cast of chapter 8.

                       These matter more to me than the rest of the repository
                       put together. Please do not copy them, trace them, use
                       them as reference, or feed them to anything. If you want
                       art like this in your game, ask a child you know to draw
                       you some. That is the whole point of them.

                       The squared-paper ground and the doodles in that folder
                       are generated by tools/art/kids_art.py and are mine, not
                       theirs; the file says which is which.

  assets/testwizard/   My own drawing, deliberately off the art contract.
  assets/enemies/      My own drawing (the Boo).


WHAT USED TO BE HERE

This repository previously contained commercial asset packs licensed for use in
a game but not for redistribution, and two music tracks whose licences could not
be established. All of it has been replaced with generated work and removed from
the repository and from its history. See .ai/asset-licensing.md for the full
account.

If you find anything in this repository that you believe is yours and should not
be here, open an issue and it will be removed.
